N:The oldest words are under the notes; Ceiriog's are the best known.
M:4/4
L:1/8
K:F
"F"c3 B A2 G2 | "Dm"F2 G2 "F"A2 F2 |
w: O mor gyn-nes | myn-wes mein-wen,
"C"GABG "F"A3 G | "F/C"F2 "C"E2 "F"F4 ||
w: fa-la-la-la-la la- | la-la-la,
"F"c3 B A2 G2 | "Dm"F2 G2 "F"A2 F2 |
w: O mor fwyn yw | llwyn meill-ion-en,
"C"GABG "F"A3 G | "F/C"F2 "C7"E2 "F"F4 ||
w: fa-la-la-la-la la- | la-la-la,
"C"G3 A "C7"B2 G2 | "F"A3 B c2 G2 |
w: O mor fel-us | yw'r cus-an-au
AB c2 "Dm"de f2 | "C"e2 "G"d2 "C7"c4 ||
w: fa-la-la fa-la-la | la-la-la,
"F/A"c3 B "F"A2 G2 | "Dm"F2 G2 "F"A2 F2 |
